# Documentation structure

Keep docs in this tree; do not dump new `.md` files into `docs/` root (except `README.md`).

| Kind | Path | Name |
|---|---|---|
| System design SSOT | `docs/architecture/` | `ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| UI/UX | `docs/design/` | thematic files |
| Plans, standards, tests | `docs/development/` | `UPPER_SNAKE.md` |
| Long-lived architecture choice | `docs/adr/` | `ADR-NNNN-slug.md` |
| Iteration / local choice | `docs/decisions/` | `DEC-NNNN-slug.md` |
| What shipped + how to verify | `docs/status/` | `STATUS-topic.md` |
| API/event contracts | `docs/contracts/` | only when stable |
| Ops runbooks | `docs/operations/` | only with real content |

## Rules

- Prefer updating `architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md` over inventing parallel design docs.
- ADR: context → decision → alternatives → consequences; never rewrite accepted ADR in place — supersede.
- DEC for pragmatic iteration choices; link related `STATUS-*.md`.
- After add/move: update `docs/README.md` and folder indexes (`status/README.md`, `decisions/README.md`).
- Use relative links inside the repo; never `Downloads/` or absolute machine paths.
- Do not create empty “future” folders; create the folder with the first real file.
